> This is my 2nd BoH explosion, is there anything I can do to prevent
> the disastrous typo again?

Some folks here give this advice; don't pick up wands of cancellation,
always leave them alone.

Since I pick up quite everything my advice differs. I put that wand in
inventory slot 'c' (and 'd', 'e', etc. if I have more than one of those
wands) preceeding any other wand in the inventory list. Then I put in
items into the BoH using the "item class" commands, and avoid single
letters; i.e. if I want to put in all scrolls and potions I just type
the letters ? and ! and all scrolls and potions will be auto-selected.
With wands I always double-check my actions. Then (playing on NAO) I
use menu colors and have wands of cancellation, bags of holdings, and
bags of tricks highlighted in a bright color (yellow or orange are good
candidates, red is a bit dark IMO). Works for me.

